esign perfection.", "timestamp_created": 1748608898, "timestamp_updated": 1783450112, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1738246187", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "195975425", "author": {"steamid": "76561197983920174", "personaname": "Supertorresmo", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/supertorresmo/", "num_games_owned": 495, "num_reviews": 233, "playtime_forever": 4324, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1822, "last_played": 1752080048, "avatar": "0ec0d5c55e1c8e052faaae58c9d172503a1728fe"}, "language": "english", "review": "This game is basically a standalone expansion for Sniper Elite 5. But I found it just as good. If you liked that game and want more, I recommend it.\n\nI have played all the Sniper Elite games, and this one is really on par with the rest. Some user reviews say this is not as good as 5, but I think it is just game fatigue. It is good when we have some mechanic changes to shake things up, and this one does not change anything, even the collectibles are the same type; but for me, it is all good because I liked the game's formula, and the more, the merrier. There is at least a new challenge game mode, so there is some difference from 5.", "timestamp_created": 1748607557, "timestamp_updated": 1748607994, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 3, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.529288709163665771", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1738246187", "reactions": []}]}